      "dom_id": "question-181722",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,|2n|>5}$\n- $B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,|2q|>5}$\n- $C={x\\in R\\,:\\,|2x|>5}$",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements. \n\nWe start by solving the following inequality for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x|>5 \\\\ 2|x|>5 \\\\ |x|>\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\nx<-\\frac{5}{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nand can be expressed as $x\\in I=(-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2})\\cup (\\frac{5}{2},\\infty ).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. If $n\\in Z,$ the solutions to the inequality $|2n|>5$ are all the integers that lie in the interval $I.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nA={…,-4,-3}\\cup {3,4,…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. If $q\\in Q,$ the solutions to $|2q|>5$ are all the rational numbers that lie in the interval $I.$ Since any real interval of nonzero length contains infinitely many rational numbers, it follows that $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊂C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,B,$ and $C.$\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-181722\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">5.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"181722\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Which of the following sets are infinite?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"119\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2208\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2124 TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-texatom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=