lass=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace></mstyle><mo>:</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace></mstyle><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </li></ol></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sun, Oct 11th @ 11:46 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:12</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-181666",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡n=0}$\n- $B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡q=0}$\n- $C={x\\in R\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0}$\n\nHint: The arguments of the trigonometric functions are in radians.",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\nWe start by writing down the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0$ for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=m\\pi ,\\,m\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is finite. There is the only value $m=0$ such that $m\\pi \\in Z.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nA={0}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|A|=1,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. Similar to the above, there is the only value $m=0$ such that $m\\pi \\in Q.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nB={0}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|B|=1,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Listing the elements of $C$ for different values of $m,$ we have\n\n$$\nC={…,-\\pi ,0,\\pi ,2\\pi ,…}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-181666\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">6.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"181666\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Which of the following sets are infinite?</p>\n<p></p><ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"142\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2208\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2124 TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</