class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2208\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub space=\"4\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2115 TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-s3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7D TEX-S3\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-mrow></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">{</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><msup><mtext>d</mtext><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace></mstyle><mo>:</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">N</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">}</mo></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </li></ol></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sun, Oct 11th @ 11:49 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:15</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-181706",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $B={{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(-\\sqrt{x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $C={{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & =\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}})=\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}} \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}})=-\\frac{6}{25\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}},\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}},-\\frac{6}{25\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is also infinite. Similar to the previous case, listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =-\\sqrt{x} \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\sqrt{x})=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}} \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nB={-\\sqrt{x},-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}},\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is also infinite. Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})=\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nC={\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
